# Pickleball Local Single Source

## Law

When building or debugging Pickleball program pages locally, treat:

`Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/testing/local-page/`

as the single local source of truth.

## Required Pattern

- Edit the `testing/local-page/` file that matches the page being previewed.
- Do not mirror, copy, sync, promote, or overwrite local-page from staging/live/root folders unless Sam explicitly asks for that exact operation.
- `npm run local-test` must only serve the local-page site. It must not rewrite files.
- `npm run local-test:sync` must not copy staging/live into local-page.
- If a requested page exists in multiple Pickleball trees, ask or infer from the browser path. For localhost previews under `/testing/local-page/`, work only in `testing/local-page/`.

## Deployment

Production or staging propagation is a separate explicit task. Do not update staging/live/root copies just because local-page changed.
